WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:11.800
Dewi wants a scholarship abroad. On her wall there is one line: improve my English.

2
00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:17.900
That is a wish. You cannot calculate a gap for a wish.

3
00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:24.400
A solid goal has three parts. What: a language test score of 6.5.

4
00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:28.100
By when: the first of March.

5
00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:33.000
And under which conditions: without leaving her part-time job.

6
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Now the gap is a number. Today she scores 5.5. At her current pace she reaches 5.9. The gap is 0.6.

7
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:51.000
She stacks her plan as a pyramid. On top, the conclusion: I can close the gap by the first of March.

8
00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:57.100
Underneath, the reasons that must add up to it: writing, listening, speaking.

9
00:00:57.100 --> 00:01:02.400
Then she checks each reason with data: two timed tests.

10
00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:08.500
Writing and listening hold. Speaking does not improve when she practises alone.

11
00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:16.600
If the reasons do not add up, there is no plan yet. She needs a speaking partner.

12
00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:25.100
For speaking she has two options. A plain list of pros and cons would favour the cheaper course.

13
00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:33.200
So she lists criteria that come from the goal, and gives them weights. Speaking practice weighs most.

14
00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:38.900
Fitting her work hours comes second, because that was her condition.

15
00:01:38.900 --> 00:01:41.900
Cost comes third.

16
00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:46.400
Weighted, the online tutor wins: sixteen to eleven.

17
00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:54.500
Before she commits, she challenges her own conclusion. She asks a senior who won the same scholarship.

18
00:01:54.500 --> 00:02:03.500
One conversation gives her a fact that a week of worrying never did: the interview matters as much as the score.

19
00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:09.200
A goal without a gap you can count is a wish.

20
00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:14.500
Criteria come from the goal. Weights come from the criteria.

21
00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:23.000
Now it is your turn. Write one goal with what, by when and conditions. Then calculate the gap.
